WEBVTT

00:01.700 --> 00:04.665
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:04.700 --> 00:07.966
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:08.000 --> 00:11.466
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:11.500 --> 00:14.467
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:14.501 --> 00:18.035
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:18.069 --> 00:21.268
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:21.302 --> 00:23.090
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:23.124 --> 00:24.923
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:24.958 --> 00:29.094
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:35.226 --> 00:38.080
I was very brave when the doctor
gave me that shot,

00:38.200 --> 00:38.854
wasn't I, Lois?

00:38.993 --> 00:40.758
Yes, Peter, you
were very brave.

00:40.793 --> 00:43.193
Even when I knew that he was
gonna give me the shot,

00:43.259 --> 00:45.060
I just k-kept looking
at him in the eye

00:45.094 --> 00:47.093
and talking to him
about my summer plans.

00:47.127 --> 00:48.560
You did very good.

00:48.594 --> 00:50.194
See, Peter? It
wasn't so bad.

00:50.228 --> 00:51.895
Yeah, except for
having to sit next to

00:51.928 --> 00:54.195
that screaming autistic lady
in the waiting room.

01:05.165 --> 01:07.798
I don't know what you want!
I don't know how to help!

01:08.832 --> 01:10.131
Hi, there. Excuse me.

01:10.166 --> 01:12.431
I seem to be lost.
Can you guys help me?

01:12.465 --> 01:13.699
Oh, my God.

01:13.733 --> 01:15.232
Are you Ryan Reynolds?

01:15.266 --> 01:16.865
<i>From The Proposal
and The Change-Up</i>

01:16.900 --> 01:19.000
and a ton of upcoming stuff?
Yeah, that's me.

01:19.034 --> 01:21.633
I was on my way to Newport
and I kind of got turned around.

01:21.667 --> 01:24.633
Ofourse, Mr. Reynolds, we'd be
happy to give you directions.

01:24.668 --> 01:26.568
You take 138
to the Jamestown Bridge,

01:26.601 --> 01:27.901
and you're gonna follow the...

01:27.935 --> 01:28.935
There's a fire truck.

01:28.969 --> 01:30.102
Yes, I see it, Peter.

01:30.136 --> 01:31.335
It's a fire truck.

01:31.369 --> 01:33.069
And after the bridge,
just follow the signs.

01:33.103 --> 01:34.102
Thanks.

01:34.136 --> 01:35.468
Hey, what happened to your arm?

01:35.503 --> 01:37.969
I just went to the doctor,
got my cholesterol checked.

01:38.004 --> 01:39.771
Wow, why does a guy in his 20s

01:39.806 --> 01:41.305
need to get his
cholesterol checked?

01:41.339 --> 01:42.738
Oh, come on, now.

01:42.772 --> 01:44.505
Oh, hey, I never got your name.

01:44.539 --> 01:45.638
Uh, Peter.
Peter Griffin.

01:45.673 --> 01:46.638
And I'm Lo...

01:46.673 --> 01:48.106
Catch you later, Peter.

01:49.074 --> 01:50.406
Wow, he was really nice.

01:50.440 --> 01:53.074
Not like when I met
that bitch Shelley Duvall.

01:54.141 --> 01:55.674
Hi, I'm Shelley Duvall.

01:55.709 --> 01:56.874
Very nice to meet you.

01:56.909 --> 01:58.241
Big deal.

01:58.275 --> 02:00.909
Came right up to me, like
I was just dying to meet her.

02:00.943 --> 02:03.042
Peter, you're gonna
have to let that one go.

02:08.578 --> 02:11.044
Hi, Mrs. Janetti.
I'm here to pick up Stewie.

02:11.079 --> 02:13.511
Oh, sure, Brian. He's in
the playroom with Gavin.

02:13.545 --> 02:15.878
Gavin- that's
a stupid name.

02:15.913 --> 02:17.678
And nobody likes you at school.

02:17.713 --> 02:19.478
You're gonna be ugly
when you grow up.

02:19.513 --> 02:21.212
And everything
in your house is cheap.

02:21.246 --> 02:22.713
And it smells in here.

02:22.747 --> 02:23.946
Oh, hey, Brian.

02:23.980 --> 02:24.946
Bye!

02:28.481 --> 02:29.547
That was fun.

02:29.582 --> 02:31.015
I like Gavin.

02:31.049 --> 02:33.082
Oh, yay!
This is such a great song.

02:34.649 --> 02:36.348
Really?
Yeah, really.

02:36.382 --> 02:38.515
I don't have to defend
Carrie Underwood to you.

02:38.549 --> 02:40.783
She is doing
just fine without you.

02:44.518 --> 02:47.284
Brian, I'm just going to sit
in the car till the song's over.

02:47.319 --> 02:49.419
All right, but don't take to
long; it'll drain the battery.

02:49.453 --> 02:51.452
Oh, shut up.
It's not draining the battery.

02:53.486 --> 02:57.120
♪ I took a Louisville Slugger
to both headlights ♪

02:57.154 --> 03:00.321
♪ I slashed a hole
in all four tires ♪

03:00.355 --> 03:04.388
♪ Maybe next time he'll think
before he cheats ♪

03:04.423 --> 03:06.622
<i>I should be on Glee.</i>

03:06.656 --> 03:08.288
<i>I should be on Glee!</i>

03:08.323 --> 03:10.823
♪ I might've saved a little
trouble for the next girl... ♪

03:11.791 --> 03:12.824
Oh, my God.

03:12.858 --> 03:14.590
I just drove.

03:14.624 --> 03:15.890
That was amazing.

03:15.925 --> 03:17.357
I can drive!

03:17.391 --> 03:21.058
Now I can do a slow cruise past
my ex-girlfriend's apartment.

03:22.526 --> 03:24.926
11:45 and the lights are on.

03:24.960 --> 03:27.093
Doing it with
the lights on now, whore?

03:27.127 --> 03:28.927
<i>Don't mind looking at his body?</i>

03:28.961 --> 03:30.993
I love you so much, though.

03:35.162 --> 03:38.561
Lois, that dog with the
different colored eyes is back.

03:38.596 --> 03:39.661
Ew, and gross!

03:39.696 --> 03:41.329
It looks like he's got a boner.

03:41.363 --> 03:42.696
Peter, just leave him alone.

03:42.731 --> 03:44.429
No, this is
what Bob Barker's been

03:44.463 --> 03:47.163
talking about all these years.

03:47.198 --> 03:48.163
Go on! Get!

03:48.198 --> 03:49.797
Get out of here,
weird boner dog!

03:50.866 --> 03:53.132
Hey, look who it is!

03:53.166 --> 03:54.298
Hey, Ryan Reynolds.

03:54.333 --> 03:55.733
What are you doing
in Cleveland's house?

03:55.767 --> 03:57.600
Well, believe it or not,
they've decided

03:57.634 --> 04:00.134
to shoot my movie
in Quahog instead of Newport.

04:00.168 --> 04:02.534
I'm playing Hitler,
but he's a young Hitler

04:02.568 --> 04:04.300
and he's got a rocking body.

04:04.335 --> 04:05.400
<i>It's called Hotler.</i>

04:05.435 --> 04:07.635
Ha! Color me seven
bucks lighter.

04:07.669 --> 04:09.702
Hey, I'm so excited
that we're gonna be neighbors.

04:09.737 --> 04:10.969
We should totally hang out.

04:11.003 --> 04:12.402
Yeah, that'd be great.

04:12.437 --> 04:14.837
Okay, I'm embarrassed.

04:14.871 --> 04:17.037
I'm standing out here
without a shirt on

04:17.071 --> 04:20.303
and my pajama bottoms are
riding insanely low on my hips.

04:20.338 --> 04:22.138
Hey, how much money you make?

04:22.172 --> 04:23.772
You'd think enough
for a shirt, right?

04:25.006 --> 04:26.571
So I'm having this
housewarming thing tonight,

04:26.606 --> 04:28.305
and I'd love it if you came by.

04:29.707 --> 04:32.006
Anything beats what goes on
at my house Friday nights.

04:33.108 --> 04:34.687
Hey, Lois, what's
going on here?

04:34.721 --> 04:36.287
Oh, it's my book club, Peter.

04:36.322 --> 04:37.288
Come join us.

04:37.323 --> 04:38.455
Oh, okay!

04:45.190 --> 04:48.557
All right, let's see,
new novel, new novel, new novel.

04:48.591 --> 04:51.058
What's it about?
What's it about?

04:51.092 --> 04:52.690
A guy...

04:52.724 --> 04:55.259
a guy who loses everything,

04:55.293 --> 04:58.859
but finds his soul in Canada.

04:58.893 --> 05:00.660
All right, we're cooking now.

05:00.694 --> 05:01.660
Cooking now.

05:01.694 --> 05:04.328
And the whole book
is an e-mail

05:04.362 --> 05:07.561
to his daughter, who's dead.

05:07.595 --> 05:10.128
And his name will be Norm Hull.

05:10.163 --> 05:12.295
Because he's just a normal guy.

05:12.330 --> 05:13.862
But not everybody
will get that.

05:13.896 --> 05:16.496
That's just for e scholars
a hundred years from now.

05:16.530 --> 05:19.030
Okay, Rupert,
you ready to go for a drive?

05:33.633 --> 05:35.933
Oh, my God, Rupert,
this is such a thrill.

05:35.968 --> 05:37.100
Look at me, I'm driving!

05:37.134 --> 05:38.633
I'm driving a real car!

05:38.668 --> 05:39.900
I don't believe it!

05:39.935 --> 05:41.734
Well, I'd say we need
to put on some tunes.

05:41.769 --> 05:45.235
Hey, welcome back to
Weenie and The Butt on 97.1.

05:45.270 --> 05:47.235
♪ 97.1 ♪

05:47.270 --> 05:48.535
Ooh, Weenie and The Butt.

05:48.570 --> 05:50.236
Just like the grown-ups
listen to.

05:50.271 --> 05:53.636
And that was "Baby" by Justin
Bieber featuring Ludacris,

05:53.671 --> 05:56.671
which means it's time to give
away some Justin Bieber tickets.

05:56.705 --> 05:57.838
Oh, that's right, Butt.

05:57.872 --> 06:00.705
<i>Our fifth caller
will ween those tickets.</i>

06:00.739 --> 06:02.106
Hey, you know what, Rupert?

06:02.140 --> 06:04.207
You know what I should do,
just, like, as a goof?

06:04.240 --> 06:06.906
I should try to win those Justin
Bieber tickets just so I can,

06:06.941 --> 06:09.607
like, tear them up or use them
to go to t concert.

06:11.409 --> 06:13.241
Oh, it's ringing, Rupert,
it's ringing.

06:13.276 --> 06:14.675
I'm too nervous;
they're celebrities.

06:14.709 --> 06:15.842
You talk to them.

06:26.312 --> 06:27.744
Oh, God.
Oh, my God.

06:27.778 --> 06:29.211
I'm in so much trouble.

06:29.245 --> 06:31.578
Congratulations,
you're caller number five.

06:31.612 --> 06:33.745
You're going to see
Justin Bieber!

06:33.780 --> 06:35.180
Oh, sweet Jesus!

06:35.213 --> 06:37.213
Yes! Jesse, I won!

06:37.247 --> 06:38.946
Never say never!

06:54.523 --> 06:55.588
Oh, my God.
Oh, my God.

06:55.644 --> 06:57.743
Oh, my God, Brian's gonna be
so mad at me.

06:57.778 --> 06:59.897
What am I gonna do?
Okay, it's all right.

07:00.016 --> 07:02.511
I'll just get a little bit of
paint and cover up the dents.

07:02.545 --> 07:04.545
Unattractive women
do it all the time.

07:04.579 --> 07:06.245
You look pretty today, Carol.

07:06.280 --> 07:07.414
Thanks.

07:07.447 --> 07:09.781
It's probably just
the dress and the makeup.

07:09.815 --> 07:11.213
Ah, now that I look closer,

07:11.247 --> 07:13.147
yeah, I think that's
what it is, too.

07:15.749 --> 07:18.048
Hey, you made it!

07:18.082 --> 07:19.315
And you brought a friend.

07:19.349 --> 07:20.315
Great.

07:20.349 --> 07:21.716
I'm his wife, Lois.

07:21.750 --> 07:23.149
We actually met the other day.

07:23.183 --> 07:25.016
Oh, sorry,
I- I meet so many people.

07:25.050 --> 07:27.050
But there's really no way
you could know that.

07:27.084 --> 07:28.384
Yeah, she's a housewife,
she don't know.

07:28.419 --> 07:29.384
Whatever.

07:29.419 --> 07:31.418
You got booze in here?

07:31.452 --> 07:33.484
Is it me, or did she
just make that weird?

07:33.519 --> 07:35.285
Please. It was
definitely not you.

07:35.319 --> 07:36.752
Hey, is this shirt too tight?

07:36.787 --> 07:37.752
I'm feeling really
self-conscious.

07:37.787 --> 07:39.119
No, not at all.

07:39.153 --> 07:41.085
So it-it looks good like
this? Yeah, it looks good.

07:41.120 --> 07:42.086
Thanks.

07:42.121 --> 07:43.686
I don't know what to say.

07:43.721 --> 07:44.853
Hey, I got, I got, like,

07:44.888 --> 07:46.754
an insider Hollywood
question for you.

07:46.789 --> 07:49.422
Is, um, is "L.A."
short for something?

07:49.456 --> 07:51.154
Ha! You're a riot.

07:51.188 --> 07:53.088
Hey, hey, so what's
all this about,

07:53.123 --> 07:55.122
everyone in Quahog
likes to tickle fight?

07:55.156 --> 07:56.355
What is that?

07:56.390 --> 07:57.623
What? I never heard that.

07:57.657 --> 07:59.223
Yeah, apparently
it's, like, a thing.

07:59.257 --> 08:00.457
It is?
Yeah.

08:00.491 --> 08:02.356
I mean, they also said
that people who pretend

08:02.391 --> 08:04.124
not to have heard
of it are chicken.

08:04.158 --> 08:05.558
Well, I ain't no chicken.

08:05.592 --> 08:07.357
One-nothing!

08:07.392 --> 08:08.625
No, two-nothing!

08:10.092 --> 08:11.059
Three-nothing!

08:11.093 --> 08:12.560
Fight over!
Fight over!

08:12.594 --> 08:14.727
Wow, you got a lot
of catching up to do,

08:14.761 --> 08:16.193
and tomorrow night
in the dark, huh?

08:16.228 --> 08:17.193
In the dark?

08:17.228 --> 08:18.461
Yeah, if you say so.

08:18.495 --> 08:20.194
Just don't tickle me
in my lower abdomen.

08:20.229 --> 08:21.595
I'm super ticklish there.

08:21.630 --> 08:23.529
<i>Lower abdomen.</i>

08:23.563 --> 08:26.029
<i>You're gonna wish
you never said that.</i>

08:26.063 --> 08:28.229
This might be
totally off the wall,

08:28.263 --> 08:31.397
but are you doing
anything Thursday night?

08:31.432 --> 08:33.030
You probably have
plans, anyway.

08:33.064 --> 08:34.397
You know what...

08:34.432 --> 08:35.898
Forget it, forget
it, forget it.

08:35.932 --> 08:37.432
Blah. Nervous.

08:38.599 --> 08:40.765
You know, Ryan,
most people take one look at me

08:40.800 --> 08:43.733
and just assume that I have
plans, so I never get asked out.

08:43.767 --> 08:46.567
But I-I frequently
don't have plans, so yes,

08:46.600 --> 08:48.634
I would love to do something
with you on Thursday night.

08:48.668 --> 08:51.334
Yes! Oh, my God, right now
would be the worst time

08:51.368 --> 08:53.000
for you to tickle
my lower abdomen,

08:53.035 --> 08:55.135
because it's so exposed
'cause I'm cheering.

08:55.169 --> 08:57.001
Yeah, Thursday night!

08:57.036 --> 08:59.235
Aw, your big mouth
just got you in trouble.

08:59.269 --> 09:00.402
Aw, I lose.

09:00.437 --> 09:02.102
Peter one, you zero.
Oh, I lose again.

09:02.137 --> 09:03.837
Peter two, you zero.
You've been practicing.

09:05.771 --> 09:09.838
We now return to the end of
a depressing 1970s sci-fi movie

09:09.872 --> 09:11.805
starring a guy in a turtleneck.

09:13.740 --> 09:15.539
We've gone far enough.

09:15.573 --> 09:17.973
I think we're safe from
The Corporation here.

09:18.007 --> 09:19.407
Adzin, ook!

09:29.811 --> 09:32.576
It can't be.

09:32.610 --> 09:34.076
No!

09:34.110 --> 09:36.510
We'll never defeat
The Corporation!

09:36.545 --> 09:38.177
They've won!

09:38.211 --> 09:40.010
There is one way, Adzin.

09:40.045 --> 09:41.611
You can shoot yourself.

09:41.646 --> 09:45.612
If it's the only way, I must.

10:08.284 --> 10:09.484
What the hell?!

10:09.518 --> 10:12.017
Stewie, get out here!

10:12.052 --> 10:13.884
Look at this.

10:13.919 --> 10:15.217
Do you know anything
about this?

10:15.252 --> 10:16.251
A- About what?

10:16.285 --> 10:17.752
About what
a beautiful day it...

10:17.786 --> 10:20.785
Oh, my God, that is surprising.

10:20.820 --> 10:23.187
Oh, I had to stop that
last sentence in the middle

10:23.221 --> 10:24.421
because I was so surprised.

10:24.456 --> 10:26.187
What happened?
Gee, I don't know.

10:26.221 --> 10:27.321
Do you know what happened?

10:28.355 --> 10:29.521
I'm sorry, w-what was that?

10:29.556 --> 10:31.155
I- I was laughing
at that funny thing

10:31.189 --> 10:32.656
you said at dinner
the other night.

10:32.690 --> 10:33.522
What funny thing?

10:33.557 --> 10:36.089
Um, y-you remember
what you said

10:36.123 --> 10:38.757
about Lois's, um,
"patoes au rotten"?

10:38.791 --> 10:41.324
Huh. Didn't ink
anybody heard that.

10:41.358 --> 10:42.691
Wish you'd laughed at the time.

10:42.725 --> 10:44.291
W- What the hell
happened to my car?!

10:44.326 --> 10:46.625
Well, I don't know, man,
but the good news is,

10:46.660 --> 10:48.625
it-it doesn't look
all that bad, Brian.

10:48.660 --> 10:50.959
It's just,
it's that spot right there

10:50.993 --> 10:52.225
that's upsetting you, right?

10:52.260 --> 10:54.593
Stewie, I know it was you.

10:58.462 --> 11:00.594
Your potato joke was terrible.

11:00.628 --> 11:02.361
I can't believe
you drove my car!

11:02.395 --> 11:03.929
You could have
gotten yourself killed!

11:03.963 --> 11:05.795
I'm gonna have to tell
Peter and Lois.

11:05.830 --> 11:07.128
No! No, you can't tell them!

11:07.163 --> 11:08.429
I'll be in so much trouble!

11:08.464 --> 11:09.596
Stewie, I have to.

11:09.630 --> 11:11.196
All right,
I have covered for you

11:11.230 --> 11:12.930
plenty of times before,
but not this time.

11:12.964 --> 11:14.129
This is very dangerous,

11:14.164 --> 11:16.465
and have to make sure
you never do it again.

11:16.499 --> 11:17.698
I won't, I swear!

11:22.166 --> 11:24.098
Stewie, calm down.

11:24.132 --> 11:27.233
Sometimes in life you just have
to accept what's coming to you.

11:27.268 --> 11:29.233
Like the contestant
who gets the lesser showcase

11:29.268 --> 11:30.534
<i>on The Price is Right.</i>

11:30.569 --> 11:32.435
Lindsay, your showcase

11:32.470 --> 11:34.769
is all about relaxation.

11:34.803 --> 11:39.736
And what better place to relax
than in your brand-new hammock?!

11:39.771 --> 11:42.670
This sturdy and portable hammock
from Swingway turns any patio

11:42.704 --> 11:44.971
into a tropical paradise.

11:45.005 --> 11:47.637
And you can entertain yourself
on your patio

11:47.672 --> 11:49.638
by drawing with chalk!

11:49.673 --> 11:52.105
Yes, Pratt and Millwood
eight-color pastel chalk

11:52.139 --> 11:55.305
will turn your patio
into a tropical art studio.

11:55.340 --> 11:57.073
But you'll have
to pack your chalk

11:57.107 --> 11:58.540
because you're going
to be staying

11:58.575 --> 12:00.039
six days and seven nights

12:00.074 --> 12:03.608
at your parents' house
in Wilmington, Delaware!

12:03.642 --> 12:06.407
I moved my abortion for this.

12:08.843 --> 12:10.809
♪ ♪

12:12.677 --> 12:16.209
Um, hey, thanks for taking
me out to dinner, Ryan,

12:16.243 --> 12:18.977
but I got to say, this
food looks a little weird.

12:19.011 --> 12:20.811
Aw, Peter, Moroccan food
is the jizz.

12:20.846 --> 12:24.378
I don't know. Looks like it
might give me the kind of farts

12:24.412 --> 12:25.978
I get from eating Mexican food.

12:27.880 --> 12:33.247
<i>Con cuidado es el stinko!</i>

12:35.115 --> 12:36.615
Hey, do these pants
look all right?

12:36.649 --> 12:39.349
Sometimes I put them on, and
I'm thinking I look all balls.

12:39.383 --> 12:40.549
No, I think you're good.

12:40.584 --> 12:41.883
You think my balls are good?

12:41.917 --> 12:43.382
You're so weird.

12:43.416 --> 12:44.816
It's awesome, though.

12:44.851 --> 12:46.350
Oh, I... I don't know.

12:46.384 --> 12:47.584
Hey, have you noticed

12:47.618 --> 12:49.784
what a jerk the mailman is
in this town?

12:49.818 --> 12:52.017
Like, he said there is no way

12:52.051 --> 12:54.118
Peter Griffin
could crush a baby bird

12:54.152 --> 12:55.952
with his bare foot
while I watched.

12:55.986 --> 12:58.752
That guy talks
more crap about me.

12:59.787 --> 13:01.453
Mmm! Oh!

13:01.488 --> 13:03.520
Mmm. You got to taste
this lamb tagine.

13:03.554 --> 13:04.954
Mmm. Here.

13:04.988 --> 13:06.253
No, that... no,
that's okay.

13:06.288 --> 13:07.554
Come on, you'll love it.

13:07.589 --> 13:08.721
Eh...

13:08.755 --> 13:09.988
Just a taste.

13:17.824 --> 13:21.123
That was... intense.

13:21.157 --> 13:22.323
What you just did.

13:23.725 --> 13:25.257
Lots of...

13:25.292 --> 13:26.692
Lots of flavors.

13:26.725 --> 13:28.057
Whoops.

13:28.092 --> 13:30.492
Whoa, freeze frame!

13:30.526 --> 13:32.092
What's gonna happen next?

13:32.126 --> 13:34.158
I think I got to
go to the bathroom.

13:43.964 --> 13:45.096
What am I gonna do?

13:45.130 --> 13:46.729
I'm gonna be in so much trouble

13:46.763 --> 13:48.597
when they find out
I wrecked Brian's car!

13:48.631 --> 13:50.463
They'll probably ship me off
to Siberia.

13:50.498 --> 13:52.330
This sucks.
I hate it here.

13:52.365 --> 13:53.564
Shut up.

13:53.599 --> 13:56.298
Drink wolf milk and
watch Russian cartoons.

13:56.332 --> 14:00.264
<i>MAN WITH RUSSIAN ACCENT: We now return to
popular Russian cartoon, Shoe and Shoelace.</i>

14:00.299 --> 14:01.665
Shoe and Shoelace!

14:01.700 --> 14:03.500
One is meaningless
without the other!

14:09.568 --> 14:10.934
Well, that's it.

14:10.969 --> 14:12.201
I have nchoice.

14:12.235 --> 14:15.002
I've got to run away.

14:20.604 --> 14:22.436
Guess I'm on my own now, Rupert.

14:22.470 --> 14:23.870
It could be worse, though.

14:23.904 --> 14:25.470
At least I'm not getting stabbed

14:25.505 --> 14:27.504
by some random guy
on the street.

14:29.171 --> 14:31.105
See? It's the exact opposite.

14:31.139 --> 14:33.105
Oh! It happened anyway!

14:39.276 --> 14:41.341
Hey, Stewie, you up?

14:43.211 --> 14:45.210
What the...

14:47.611 --> 14:49.284
Brian, I've decided to run away.

14:49.404 --> 14:50.703
Don't come looking for me.

14:50.737 --> 14:53.036
And definitely don't chase me
to the airport

14:53.070 --> 14:54.504
and catch me at the gate

14:54.538 --> 14:56.671
just before I'm about
to get on the plane

14:56.705 --> 14:58.737
with, like, an emotional speech
and possibly flowers.

14:58.772 --> 15:00.204
For example, it would be awful

15:00.238 --> 15:02.405
if all the TSA people were
gathered around,

15:02.439 --> 15:03.838
watching this emotional moment,

15:03.872 --> 15:06.205
even the older black female
carry-on scanner

15:06.239 --> 15:08.406
who initially stopped you
at the baggage check,

15:08.440 --> 15:11.006
but who after you told her
of your intentions, said,

15:11.040 --> 15:13.373
"Go get him, child,"
in flagrant disregard

15:13.408 --> 15:16.675
of all newly-implemented
post-9-11 security measures.

15:16.709 --> 15:18.908
And if you were considerin
bringing a boom box

15:18.942 --> 15:22.442
to play music, I would suggest
any one of these six songs.

15:26.711 --> 15:28.143
So again, ran away.

15:28.177 --> 15:29.510
Don't come after me.

15:29.544 --> 15:34.044
♪ I want to thank you... ♪

15:38.078 --> 15:40.413
Dirty whores, all of you.

15:40.447 --> 15:41.812
Oh, hey, Peter.

15:41.846 --> 15:43.379
Lois, we got a problem.

15:43.414 --> 15:45.780
I think Ryan Reynolds
is in love with me.

15:45.814 --> 15:47.948
What? Don't be ridiculous.

15:47.982 --> 15:49.782
It's true. Last night we were
at this restaurant,

15:49.816 --> 15:51.248
and he tried to gay kiss me.

15:51.283 --> 15:53.015
I'm telling you,
he wants to get with me.

15:53.049 --> 15:54.482
Peter, come on.

15:54.517 --> 15:57.183
Why would any man dress well,
groom himself and lift weights

15:57.217 --> 15:58.750
just to sleep with other men?

15:58.785 --> 16:00.083
He's not gay.

16:00.118 --> 16:02.518
Well, I don't care what you say.
He likes me.

16:02.552 --> 16:04.584
And we do have chemistry,
I- I won't deny that.

16:04.619 --> 16:06.352
I- I... I will take
responsibility

16:06.386 --> 16:07.819
fomy part in this.

16:07.852 --> 16:10.252
I'm just gonna go over there
and let him down easy.

16:11.287 --> 16:13.920
Oh, Snooki died.

16:16.688 --> 16:17.820
Last stop.

16:20.221 --> 16:21.721
What? This isn't the airport.

16:22.955 --> 16:24.188
Oh, my God, Rupert!

16:24.222 --> 16:25.922
We've got to get out of here!

16:26.956 --> 16:28.122
Aah! Damn it!

16:28.156 --> 16:29.356
Oh, no, no.

16:29.390 --> 16:30.723
Baby fall down!

16:30.757 --> 16:32.956
Is that...? Is that Consuela?

16:34.458 --> 16:36.691
Baby all alone in street.

16:36.725 --> 16:38.024
I take baby home.

16:38.058 --> 16:39.825
It's me. Stewie.
Don't you remember?

16:39.859 --> 16:41.458
You used to clean for us.

16:41.492 --> 16:43.858
We used to make you use the
bathroom at the gas station.

16:46.527 --> 16:48.259
Hey, you!

16:48.294 --> 16:49.627
Uh, hey, Ryan.

16:49.661 --> 16:50.893
Uh, bad time?

16:50.928 --> 16:52.328
Um, perfect time.

16:52.362 --> 16:55.329
Come on in.
I was just oiling my legs.

16:55.363 --> 16:56.696
So, hey, what's on for tonight?

16:56.730 --> 16:58.530
You know, my dentist
leaves his office unlocked.

16:58.564 --> 17:00.330
I was thinking we
could do some nitrous

17:00.364 --> 17:01.630
and then have dinner in there.

17:01.664 --> 17:04.197
Look, Ryan, you're a great guy
and everything,

17:04.231 --> 17:06.731
but I don't like you
in that way.

17:06.765 --> 17:09.365
I mean, there are some things
that I would do with you,

17:09.399 --> 17:11.231
but my heart wouldn't be in it.

17:11.265 --> 17:12.898
What are you talking about?

17:12.933 --> 17:16.098
That you like me,
and you want to be my boyfriend.

17:17.400 --> 17:19.066
You think I'm gay?

17:19.100 --> 17:20.900
Where did you get that?

17:20.935 --> 17:22.867
Uh, uh, you-you tried
to kiss me.

17:22.901 --> 17:24.501
Peter, I'm not gay.

17:24.536 --> 17:26.435
What the hell's
the matter with you?

17:26.469 --> 17:29.101
Look, look, look, let me...
let me put it to you this way.

17:29.136 --> 17:30.602
I'm attracted to you in the way

17:30.637 --> 17:33.569
that a man is attracted
to a woman, but I'm not gay.

17:33.603 --> 17:35.537
When you live out in
Hollywood, you learn

17:35.571 --> 17:37.537
that life is about different
spirits and energies

17:37.571 --> 17:38.937
you meet along the way.

17:38.971 --> 17:41.705
I just thought maybe our spirits
could intertwine, you know?

17:41.739 --> 17:43.571
Ouenergies could merge.

17:43.605 --> 17:46.171
Like my spirit could go
up inside your energy.

17:46.206 --> 17:48.772
I- I have so much to learn
about show business.

17:48.807 --> 17:50.139
But you know what?

17:50.173 --> 17:51.939
I could never really be
attracted to somebody

17:51.973 --> 17:54.773
who uses labels like
"gay" and "straight."

17:54.808 --> 17:56.240
Maybe you should just go.

17:56.274 --> 17:57.541
Well-Well, now,
wait a second.

17:57.575 --> 17:58.775
What do you mean?

17:58.810 --> 17:59.908
This isn't working.

17:59.943 --> 18:01.142
It was a nice thought,

18:01.176 --> 18:03.343
but I think we should
go our separate ways.

18:03.377 --> 18:05.243
No, Ryan. I get it now.

18:05.277 --> 18:06.943
I can be what you want.

18:06.977 --> 18:08.377
We could...
Peter.

18:08.411 --> 18:09.677
Don't embarrasyourself.

18:09.712 --> 18:11.345
You need to just let this go.

18:13.045 --> 18:14.745
Tickle fight! Tickle
fight! No, Peter, no!

18:14.779 --> 18:16.679
Tickle fight! Tickle fight!
Tickle fight... Peter, no! No!

18:16.714 --> 18:18.846
Oh, my God...

18:22.881 --> 18:24.680
It's time for you to leave.

18:27.148 --> 18:29.448
I can change.

18:29.482 --> 18:31.114
I can change.

18:31.149 --> 18:32.582
I'm sorry, Peter.
We're done.

18:32.616 --> 18:34.114
We can never talk again.

18:34.149 --> 18:37.450
Here's a cell phone
so we can always talk.

18:41.984 --> 18:44.183
Don't you guys
have any tub toys?

18:44.218 --> 18:45.651
Here. Is rattle.

18:45.685 --> 18:47.751
This is prescription
medication.

18:47.785 --> 18:50.018
And it's not even
your name on the label.

18:50.053 --> 18:51.485
What... What is this?

18:51.519 --> 18:52.785
What's in this tub?

18:52.820 --> 18:54.486
Is jicama.
Jicama?

18:54.520 --> 18:56.253
And what is...?
What...? What...?

18:56.287 --> 18:57.686
This is a chicken leg.

18:57.721 --> 18:59.854
Are you also making soup?

18:59.888 --> 19:01.321
For quincea├▒era.

19:01.355 --> 19:03.154
Big party. Many peoples.

19:03.188 --> 19:04.456
Oh, my God.

19:04.490 --> 19:05.922
<i>Hay un perro aqui.</i>

19:05.957 --> 19:08.022
<i>┬┐Doggy es aqui?</i>

19:08.057 --> 19:10.957
<i>I bet even you guys
don't watch George Lopez.</i>

19:10.991 --> 19:12.890
Consuela?

19:12.924 --> 19:14.257
Hey, it's Brian.

19:14.291 --> 19:15.624
I'm-I'm looking for Stewie.

19:15.659 --> 19:17.891
<i>No, no baby aqui.</i>

19:17.925 --> 19:19.191
I peed in your soup.

19:19.226 --> 19:20.525
Happy 15th birthday.

19:20.560 --> 19:21.892
Which, by the way,

19:21.926 --> 19:24.292
is not a special occasion
in the normal world.

19:24.327 --> 19:25.560
Stewie, I've been worried sick.

19:25.594 --> 19:27.193
What the hell
are you doing here?

19:27.228 --> 19:28.693
Brian? How did you find me?

19:28.728 --> 19:31.494
I used my nose,
which I always forget about.

19:31.528 --> 19:32.661
Come on, let's go.

19:32.695 --> 19:34.362
No, I'm not going
back! I can't!

19:34.396 --> 19:35.795
They're gonna be mad at me!

19:35.830 --> 19:37.595
I didn't tell anyone.

19:37.629 --> 19:39.596
You... you didn't?

19:39.630 --> 19:40.796
No, I didn't.

19:40.831 --> 19:43.063
Look, I thought about it,
and to be honest,

19:43.097 --> 19:45.831
it's probably my fault for
leaving you alone in the car.

19:45.865 --> 19:49.064
And if you promise never to do
it again, I won't say anything.

19:49.098 --> 19:51.097
Okay, I promise.

19:51.131 --> 19:52.398
My baby!
What?

19:52.432 --> 19:53.865
I say, let go of me.

19:53.899 --> 19:54.998
Consuela, we're leaving.

19:55.032 --> 19:56.165
My baby!

19:56.199 --> 19:58.399
Hey, she says
it's her baby, man.

19:58.433 --> 19:59.999
Now, get out of here.

20:01.334 --> 20:03.800
Is my baby. Ernesto.

20:03.835 --> 20:05.300
No, I'm not...
I'm not Ernest...

20:05.335 --> 20:08.401
Okay, this is so messed up
right now.

20:15.438 --> 20:17.404
I did not want
to have to do that.

20:17.438 --> 20:20.304
They were very nice
to me up until then.

20:22.539 --> 20:24.672
Peter, stop staring
outhe window.

20:24.706 --> 20:26.105
Ryan's gone.

20:26.139 --> 20:28.138
He finished his movie,
he's moved out.

20:28.173 --> 20:30.006
How could I have been so blind?

20:30.040 --> 20:32.807
How could I not have seen
what he offered?

20:32.842 --> 20:34.774
I think the whole
thing was very strange.

20:34.808 --> 20:36.007
<i>He thought you were strange!</i>

20:36.041 --> 20:38.842
How about that?
Whatever.

20:38.876 --> 20:41.075
I just can't help but wonder...

20:41.109 --> 20:42.782
will I ever see him again?

20:42.783 --> 21:43.783
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru